## Code Safety

The real-to-candidate diff is confined to the existing first component filter
inside `line_bands`: the new scalar predicate, its inclusion in
`isolated_fragment`, and the vertical-support guard. There are no page-specific
coordinates or changes to input preparation, extraction, glyph estimation,
fraction helpers, later merging or unrelated functions.

Operator grouping is correct: support is
`(same_centre OR ((NOT sparse) AND vertical_eligibility AND vertical_gap))
AND horizontal_gap`, under the existing `not any(...)` removal condition.
The guard cannot bypass horizontal proximity or disable the centre branch.
The doubled-centre comparison allows actual centre distance0.75 glyph.
The pre-existing short-row exemption is unchanged.

The new predicate is exactly inclusive0.3..0.4 glyph height, width at least3
glyphs, and strictly below0.2 bounding-box ink density. For components outside
that class, the original removal/support expression is unchanged.

Input immutability remains structural: `line_bands` starts with `ink.copy()`,
retains a separate read-only support copy, and deletes only matching labels
through a region of the counting copy. Saved real/synthetic assertions
corroborate this; the review executes none of them.

